<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <AgoraPackageName>IoT</AgoraPackageName>
    <!--
      io.agora:iotsdk is Agora's IoT SDK — the app-side half of its camera/doorbell stack, on its
      own 1.3.x line.

      It is the odd one out in this repository in three ways, all of them the consumer's business:

      1. There is no iOS counterpart. Agora ships the IoT SDK for Android and Linux only, so
         there is no Net.Agora.IoT.iOS and no cross-platform facade in sbokatuk/Net.Agora — this
         package is the whole product.

      2. It cannot coexist with any other package here. The .aar bundles its own copies of
         agora-rtc-sdk.jar and agora-rtm-sdk.jar (plus the matching .so files), so referencing it
         alongside Net.Agora.Video.Android, Net.Agora.Voice.Android or Net.Agora.Signaling.Android
         fails at dex merge on duplicate io.agora.rtc2.* / io.agora.rtm.* classes. That is Agora's
         packaging, not this binding's.

      3. Maven Central's newest is 1.3.0, while Agora's documentation describes 1.8.0 — which is
         published only as a direct download. This package binds what is actually resolvable.

      And one more that is the consumer's problem rather than this binding's: the SDK's
      device-messaging and alarm features talk to AWS IoT Core, and io.agora:iotsdk declares no
      dependency on the AWS Android SDK — so an app using them has to supply it, and there is no
      official .NET binding for it. See Transforms/Metadata.xml.
    -->
    <AgoraGroupId>io.agora</AgoraGroupId>
    <AgoraArtifact>iotsdk</AgoraArtifact>
    <AgoraNativeVersion>$(AgoraIoTVersion)</AgoraNativeVersion>
    <VersionPrefix>$(AgoraIoTVersion).$(AgoraIoTBindingRevision)</VersionPrefix>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <Import Project="../Agora.Binding.props" />

  <!--
    The Java package is io.agora.iotlink. Renamed to Agora.IoT for the same reason as the other
    products' renames — the SDK's own C# naming is what a consumer looks for first — with the .NET
    capitalisation of the acronym rather than the Java one.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <AndroidNamespaceReplacement Include="IO.Agora.Iotlink" Replacement="Agora.IoT" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Description>.NET for Android bindings for the Agora IoT Android SDK, generated from io.agora:iotsdk $(AgoraIoTVersion) on Maven Central. Lets a .NET app pair with, call and control Agora IoT devices. Three things to know before adopting it: Android only (Agora ships no iOS IoT SDK, so there is no cross-platform client); mutually exclusive with the Video, Voice and Signaling packages, whose native artifacts it bundles its own copies of; and its device-messaging features route through AWS IoT Core, whose Android SDK has no .NET binding and would have to be supplied separately.</Description>
    <PackageTags>$(PackageTags);IoT;devices;streaming</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
